{
 "_about": "recipes for tools/assets/mouse-view.py: how the picture of a mouse with its button markers and light masks gets put together out of the sorted Swarm artwork (the folder sort-swarm.py writes). key = usb product id. device = folder in there. picture = the top view (a path that starts with another device folder is taken from there). like = start from the recipe of that pid and change what is listed. inputs = for every button in OUR order (the order rockcat_input_label counts in) the number Swarm prints on its marker, 0 for a button without a marker. view = which of the button page pictures of the device the markers come from (default 0). nudge = [x, y] pushes all markers by that much (the Kova ones sat 0.9 px left of the middle of the mouse: 0.4 from where the picture was dragged to, 0.5 from rounding). extras = more pictures on the same canvas, each {picture, at, scale} and view = the button page picture whose markers come along (the side of the Leadr), or just a picture to hang lights on (the back of the Nyth). lights = one entry per led we know: led = our led index, then either hue = [from, to] (the light is painted into the picture in that colour, angles on the colour wheel, box = [x0, y0, x1, y1] to only take it there, extras = true to take it off the extra pictures as well) or from = a light layer (of this device or one with the same shape) with scale and at to make it fit the picture, kind = luma for the grey on black ones, painted = true when the picture already shows that light in ROCCATs colours so the layer has to cover it when off too. the at / scale numbers of layers out of another picture were found by matching that picture onto the top view, not by eye",
